# Staging migration env template — copied to `docker/.env.migrate` on the
# host (gitignored). Real values are managed by the host secret-management
# agent; this file is the spec, not the source of truth.
#
# Loaded only by the one-shot `reverie-migrate` service via `env_file:` in
# compose.staging.yml. Kept separate from `staging.env.runtime.example` so
# the schema-management (DDL) credential never reaches the long-lived app
# container — in the shipped topology the app holds zero migration creds
# (adr/2026-06-02-hybrid-migration-entrypoints-and-role.md).

# Migration DSN — the least-privilege `reverie_migrator` role created by
# init-roles.sql (NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEROLE NOBYPASSRLS, owns the schema
# objects it creates). The embedded password must match
# REVERIE_MIGRATOR_PASSWORD set in `staging.env.bootstrap.example`.
DATABASE_URL_MIGRATION=postgres://reverie_migrator:<password>@reverie-postgres:5432/reverie
